Ladybird parses manifest.json in the UI process into one model for
manifest versions 2 and 3, reads the content scripts at load time,
and generates the page that hosts background scripts. WebKit’s
WebExtension::parseManifest() and its parse*Properties() helpers do
the same in the UI process, with generatedBackgroundContent() for
the background scripts and isWebAccessibleResource(requestURL,
pageURL) for resource access. Blink’s Extension::Create() runs the
manifest handlers (content_scripts_handler.cc, web_accessible_
resources_info.cc, csp_info.cc) in the browser process, generates
the background page in GenerateBackgroundPageContents() of
extension_protocols.cc, and gates resource loads with
AllowExtensionResourceLoad(). Gecko’s ExtensionData.parseManifest()
in Extension.sys.mjs produces the same shape, WebExtensionPolicy::
IsWebAccessiblePath() and SourceMayAccessPath() answer resource
access, and ExtensionProtocolHandler::AllowExternalResource() refuses
a file outside the extension directory, as Ladybird’s open_resource()
does with the file it has opened. The version-2 “permissions” list
mixing host patterns with permission names is split the way Gecko’s
ExtensionData does in parseManifest().

Ladybird refuses an encoded “/” in an extension resource path, as Blink
does in ExtensionURLToRelativeFilePath(), which decodes the path with
UnescapeBinaryURLComponentSafe() and fail_on_path_separators set.
Gecko instead decodes escaped dots and slashes before the URL is
normalized, in SubstitutingProtocolHandler::NewURI(), and then its
ResolveURI() rejects a decoded backslash.

Ladybird checks the real location of the file it opened against
the extension directory. The other engines check by path: Blink’s
ExtensionResource::GetFilePath() requires the normalized resource
to be under the normalized root, Gecko’s ExtensionProtocolHandler::
NewStream() checks nsIFile::Contains(), and WebKit’s WebExtension::
resourceFileURLForPath() compares real paths. Checking the opened
file rather than its path means a symlink swapped in after the
check can’t escape either.
